# Reading: Second Position (repertoire plan: st-read-second-position). An original reading study,
# 16 bars of 4/4, with the hand in second position the whole time: finger 1 on fret 2, finger 2 on
# fret 3, finger 3 on fret 4, finger 4 on fret 5, and no open strings.
#   Bars 1-8, A major (F#, C#, G#), on strings 3, 2 and 1: two 4-bar phrases over A, D and E7.
#   Bars 9-16, F# minor (the same key signature), on strings 6 to 3: two 4-bar phrases over
#   F#m, Bm, C#7 and D. Over C#7 the seventh note is raised to E#, written on string 4 fret 3
#   (the fret you know as F), and it leads up to F#.
# Bars 6 and 13 have a syncopation: eighth, quarter, eighth, so the quarter starts on the "and"
# of beat 1 and is held through beat 2.
# G# is taken only where second position has it (string 6 fret 4, string 1 fret 4): the G# on
# string 3 would need fret 1, so the tunes are written around it.
title: Reading: Second Position
composer: Sixstring Academy
